<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_755acacf-a128-4faa-84c4-2bc1aceaa5e5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6E"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6E</no><heading guid="_8690aeef-1ed8-4cde-bbb5-8fa6fd429be4"
id="sec.6E-he"><b>Application of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6E-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_44912f57-053b-46b0-a83c-2a3739cf45d5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6E-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act applies whether the subject-matter of
the complaint arises within or outside New South Wales, and whether the
wrongdoer, the person whose death has been caused, or any other person
concerned was or is a British subject or not.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6E-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fe733c9f-911c-4f7d-a5f4-fe79f96d47ab"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6E-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act applies to actions commenced either
before or after the commencement of the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Compensation to Relatives (Amendment)
Act 1928</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6E-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a0bc4695-8f3b-4173-a322-db042ca50d1c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6E-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act shall bind the
Crown.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 6E:</b> Ins 1928 No 8,
sec 2 (2).</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f28c6847-13cd-423f-bb10-5f9342475f91"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_183655d4-9389-4387-b59b-da0eb9565b4f"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Construction of Act</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_91633f7f-957f-41d3-829e-301bcc925cca"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following words are intended to have the
meanings hereby assigned to them respectively, so far as such meanings are not
excluded by the context or by the nature of the subject matter, that is to
say, the word <defterm type="definition"
guid="_0e6a1c28-ee42-4e5c-8270-5b78b7e479a6"
id="sec.7-def.parent"><b><i>parent</i></b></defterm> shall include father and
mother, and grandfather and grandmother, and stepfather and stepmother, and
any person standing in loco parentis to another; and the word <defterm
type="definition" guid="_5fa59eb0-5ed9-4971-9338-1a4078521c1c"
id="sec.7-def.child"><b><i>child</i></b></defterm> shall include son and
daughter, and grandson and granddaughter, and stepson and stepdaughter, and
any person to whom another stands in loco parentis; and the word <defterm
type="definition" guid="_73def82d-e603-4791-bc0f-75b9d0d37658"
id="sec.7-def.declaration"><b><i>declaration</i></b></defterm> shall include
any statement of the cause of action appropriate to the court in which the
action is brought.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1A" status="repealed">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_90df9eb9-9619-4849-a796-40f983b8c087"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1A"></attrib>
<attrib name="status" value="repealed"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1A), (1B)</no></head>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_562fa975-01f6-4ed0-a74c-4f394db29980"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act <defterm type="definition"
guid="_ec74ba25-6d37-47f3-96b9-a13667479d6d"
id="sec.7-def.administrator"><b><i>administrator</i></b></defterm> means
administrator within the meaning of the <legref refid="act-1898-013"
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Probate and
Administration Act 1898</i></name></legref> and includes the NSW Trustee and
Guardian acting as collector of an estate under an order to
collect.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5ab117e2-ec3a-464e-af6d-cf6fec5be1d1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act <defterm type="definition"
guid="_aaf46b73-dc27-4960-b2e1-f389f3fce7a7"
id="sec.7-def.executor"><b><i>executor</i></b></defterm> means the executor to
whom probate has been granted and includes an executor by right of
representation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bbbc527f-23eb-4d71-8857-09ae2ea87ef3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, <defterm type="definition"
guid="_e6da030a-f3d8-4c56-acc1-11bf6c90ed8b"
id="sec.7-def.spouse"><b><i>spouse</i></b></defterm> means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a65b97fd-93f0-44be-97b2-433be74fdf18" id="sec.7-ssec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the person to whom a person is legally married
(including the husband or wife of a person), or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8d505c18-5838-4486-8ead-d5058e98e7f7" id="sec.7-ssec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a de facto partner.</txt></block>
<note type="legtext" guid="_ad8cf9d4-33e6-410f-b667-81f215f4c451"
id="sec.7-ssec.4-para1.b-note"><heading
guid="_1f51dc6d-607e-4dfd-bb84-915a28ab5736"
id="sec.7-ssec.4-para1.b-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">&#8220;De facto partner&#8221; is defined in
section 21C of the <legref refid="act-1987-015" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Interpretation Act
1987</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></note>
</li></list>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 1928 No 8,
sec 2 (3); 1942 No 15, sec 44 (c); 1984 No 149, Sch 1 (2); 1999 No 4, Sch 2.3
[3]&#8211;[5]; 2006 No 80, Sch 3.3; 2010 No 19, Sch 3.21; 2012 No 95, Sch 2.5;
2018 No 28, Sch 1.10.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_71fde572-471f-48af-98f0-bda24ce03aa9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_bdae6fba-60b9-40d3-99db-73e236e07f66"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Rights of action in respect of past
events</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The amendments made to this Act by the <legref
refid="act-1999-004" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Property (Relationships) Legislation Amendment Act
1999</i></name></legref> do not operate to confer on any person a right of
action in relation to any act, neglect or default that took place before those
amendments took effect.</txt></block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 8:</b> Ins 1999 No 4,
Sch 2.3 [6].</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


